  "prefLabel": "Env-WC 103.05 Quorum",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-WC 103.05 Quorum.\n\n(a) A quorum of the council shall be a simple majority of the total number of sitting members, provided, however, that in the context of an appeal, a quorum shall be a simple majority of those sitting members who are not recused from the appeal.\n\n(b) The council shall take formal or official action only when a quorum is present.\n\nSource. #8976, eff 9-14-07",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wc100.html"
}
